    <briefdescription>
<para>A single point-in-time measurement, wrapping a <computeroutput>timespec</computeroutput> value. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamp" kindref="compound">timestamp</ref></computeroutput> stores one <computeroutput>timespec</computeroutput> sample obtained from the system clock. It is default-constructible (zero-initialises the <computeroutput>timespec</computeroutput>), copy-constructible, and move-constructible, so that it can be used efficiently in <computeroutput>std::optional&lt;<ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamp" kindref="compound">timestamp</ref>&gt;</computeroutput> containers.</para>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1timestamp_1ae5494fb57bcc3b577c914a0cc95ff667" kindref="member">has_clock()</ref></computeroutput> predicate allows callers to determine whether a real-time clock is available on the target platform before relying on the stored value. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
